n url={https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.10121}\n}\n\n@article{Demsar,\n title={{Statistical Comparisons of Classifiers over Multiple Data Sets}},\n author={Janez DemÅ¡ar},\n year={2006},\n journal={Journal of Machine Learning Research},\n url={https://www.jmlr.org/papers/v7/demsar06a.html}\n}\n\n@article{Cawley,\n title={{On Over-fitting in Model Selection and Subsequent Selection Bias in Performance Evaluation}},\n author={Gavin C. Cawley and Nicola L. C. Talbot},\n year={2010},\n journal={Journal of Machine Learning Research},\n url={https://www.jmlr.org/papers/v11/cawley10a.html}\n}\n\n@article{Huber,\n title={{Robust Estimation of a Location Parameter}},\n author={Peter J. Huber},\n year={1964},\n journal={The Annals of Mathematical Statistics},\n doi={10.1214/aoms/1177703732}\n}\n\n@article{Efron,\n title={{Bootstrap Methods: Another Look at the Jackknife}},\n author={B. Efron},\n year={1979},\n journal={The Annals of Statistics},\n doi={10.1214/aos/1176344552}\n}\n# Global Memory Summary\n\nUse as qualitative context only; do not use as quantitative grounding source.\n\n## Recent Entries\n\n- 2026-11-17 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Selected Certified Attainability Frontiers for Targeted Leaderboard Investment; wrote matching idea and rubric bundles. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Only an untested proposal and the supplied incumbent aggregate are available, so no evidence-backed distilled recommendation is added.\n  - evidence: Supplied bootstrap correct=true and combined_score=0.53012102014295; no recent ideas or attempts. Named external incumbent source was unavailable; implementation details and failure causes remain unknown. Alternatives were perfect-score-only attacks, unsupported training-cost curves, and a wider aggregation-rule catalogue. Bounded score-response ceilings permit exact support-cost certificates using documented public score matrices. No experiments or literature searches were run. Only canonical local memory path ideas/01_certified_at